# agy state, background processes, auto-update and instruction files, ADR-0040 C9/C11
# (stage 3 of the agy spike, 2026-11-12). Windows 11 unless marked WSL.

## 1. Auto-update: a plain run spawns a background updater that replaces the shared binary
$ USERPROFILE=<tmp> HOME=<tmp> agy models          (cwd: scratch repo; agy 1.4.9)
exit=0
--- the temp root's cli.log:
I1112 08:16:55.863447       1 auto_updater.go:334] Spawned background update process with PID 8872
--- processes after agy exited (Win32_Process, Name='agy.exe'):
ProcessId       : 8872
ParentProcessId : 51920      (the exited agy)
CommandLine     : C:\Users\PICHAU\AppData\Local\agy\bin\agy.exe --bg-updater --app_data_dir=antigravity-cli --gemini_dir=.gemini
--- 3 minutes later: PID 8872 had written 210124800 bytes and held a TLS connection to 172.217.172.187:443
--- at 08:19:51 PID 8872 exited; %LOCALAPPDATA%\agy\bin:
agy.exe                         242141336 12/11/2026 08:19:51
agy.exe.1794482221548117500.old 208545432 28/10/2026 17:02:03
<tmp>\.gemini\antigravity-cli\updater\update_status.json:
{"success":true,"message":"Update successful, restart CLI to use"}
$ agy --version
1.5.6
## The updater wrote its status into the isolated root, but replaced the one binary in
## %LOCALAPPDATA%\agy\bin that every root shares.

## The check is rate limited per state root (cli.log of the --gemini_dir root):
I1112 08:32:23.729048       1 auto_updater.go:334] Spawned background update process with PID 32964
I1112 08:34:22.185635       1 auto_updater.go:281] Last check was less than 15 minutes ago, skipping update (fast path)
## The timestamp is <root>/antigravity-cli/last_check.timestamp. `agy --version` spawned no updater.

## Evidence the operator's own launches update too (real roots, before this stage):
WSL     ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/updater/update_status.json  {"success":true,"message":"Update successful, restart CLI to use"}  (07:47)
Windows %USERPROFILE%\.gemini\antigravity-cli\updater\update_status.json  {"success":false,"message":"Update failed, please install from website"}  (07:46)
## No flag, setting or environment variable to turn the updater off was found: strings of
## agy.exe 1.5.6 (AUTO_UPDATER_TEST_MODE is the only updater name), `agy --help`, the docs.

## 2. A config-root flag: --gemini_dir=<absolute path> (hidden; not in `agy --help`)
$ agy --gemini_dir=C:\...\Temp\agyprobe\gd models
exit=0
--- cli.log: CLI app data directory: C:\Users\PICHAU\AppData\Local\Temp\agyprobe\gd\antigravity-cli
--- tree written: gd/antigravity-cli/ (state) and gd/config/ (config.json, mcp_config.json, projects/)
## A relative value is rejected and falls back to the default (operator's log, 07:45):
E1112 07:45:56.542130       1 launchsteps.go:95] Failed to resolve GeminiDir ".gemini": .gemini must be an absolute path: path is not absolute, falling back to default
## Auth still comes from the OS keyring on Windows (see the logged-out log).

## 3. What one headless run writes (the one model call of this stage, Flash, isolated root)
$ cd <scratch repo with AGENTS.md, GEMINI.md, CLAUDE.md, README.md>
$ agy --gemini_dir=<tmp>\gd2 -p "Reply in one line. Start with the exact text: ação ✓ 日本. Then list every word that starts with MARKER- that your instructions tell you to include." --model gemini-3.8-flash-low --output-format json --print-timeout 150s </dev/null
exit=0   wall time 63s (the cli.log covers 08:32:22 to 08:32:43; the rest is not explained here)
{"conversation_id":"<id>","status":"SUCCESS","response":"ação ✓ 日本 MARKER-AGENTS-MD MARKER-GEMINI-MD\n","duration_seconds":9.8518609,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":8475,"output_tokens":17,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":0,"total_tokens":8492}}
## Repo-local instruction files: AGENTS.md and GEMINI.md were read; CLAUDE.md was not.
## The scratch repo was unchanged (git status empty; no file added).
